  // arm64/AST keep the register-ABI hand-asm.
  // __fern_remove_file is now a Fern runtime function (#2649): emitted via
  // emit_ir_runtime_fern_fn in the entry block (need-gated on remove_file) —
  // unlinkat via __syscall3, returns Result[(), IoError]. The op_remove_file handler
  // calls the stack-ABI __fn___fern_remove_file symbol.
  // __fern_temp_dir is now a Fern runtime function (#2649): emitted via
  // emit_ir_runtime_fern_fn in the entry block (need-gated on temp_dir) — builds
  // /tmp/<prefix>-<monotonic_ns> with the raw intrinsics, mkdirat via __syscall3,
  // returns Result[string, IoError]. Calls the (Fern) monotonic_ns helper. The
  // op_temp_dir handler calls the stack-ABI __fn___fern_temp_dir symbol.
  // __fern_read_dir is now a Fern runtime function (#2649): emitted via
  // emit_ir_runtime_fern_fn in the fs bundle (need-gated on read_dir) — drains the
  // directory with a getdents64 loop over a fresh 64 KiB buffer per read, building
  // a string[] with .append(). The op-171 handler calls the stack-ABI
  // __fn___fern_read_dir symbol; arm64/AST keep the register-ABI hand-asm.
  // __fern_env: %rdi = name string box -> Option[string] box. Walks __fern_envp
  // (saved by the entry's _start, gated on the same env need) for an entry whose
  // key matches name + '=', and boxes the value (kernel-immortal bytes, no copy).
  // Transcribed verbatim from asm.fern's emit_runtime (the same body the AST path
  // called); gated on the env need; calls __fern_alloc (the heap runtime, present).
  // __fern_envp (.bss) is read by both __fern_env and __fern_subprocess (execve's
  // envp), and saved by _start; declare it ONCE when either need is present.
  if (s.any_need(["env", "subprocess", "environ", "raw_environ"])) {
    s = s.write(".section .bss\n");
    s = s.write("    .align 8\n");
    s = s.write("__fern_envp: .quad 0\n");
    s = s.write(".section .text\n");
  }
  // __fern_env is now a Fern runtime function (#2649): emitted via
  // emit_ir_runtime_fern_fn in the entry block (need-gated on env) — walks the
  // envp array (via __raw_environ, reading the __fern_envp global declared
  // above) and copies the matched value. The op_env handler calls the stack-ABI
  // __fn___fern_env symbol.
  // __fern_stat is now a Fern runtime function (#2649): emitted via
  // emit_ir_runtime_fern_fn in the entry block (need-gated on stat) — the
  // first syscall leaf returning a user-typed Result[FileStat, IoError]. It
  // stat(2)s into __fern_scratch via __syscall3, reads st_mode/st_size, and
  // builds Ok(FileStat{...}) / Err(NotFound(path)). The op_stat handler calls
  // the stack-ABI __fn___fern_stat symbol.
  // __fern_subprocess is now a Fern runtime function (#2649): emitted via
  // emit_ir_runtime_fern_fn in the migrated-helpers section (need-gated on
  // subprocess) — three pipes, fork, execve with the /bin and /usr/bin
  // fallbacks in the child, stdin feed + stream drain + wait4 in the parent,
  // returning a ProcessResult built by the ordinary struct lowering. The
  // op-177 handler calls the stack-ABI __fn___fern_subprocess symbol.
  // __fern_argc / __fern_argv globals (.bss) + __fern_arg_at + __fern_args: the
  // command-line argv accessor. The entry's _start saves argc / argv from the
  // initial stack into these globals (gated on the same args need); __fern_args
  // builds a cap-header string[] of one __fern_arg_at box per argument. Gated on
  // the args need; calls __fern_str_box + __fern_arr_box (the heap runtime,
  // already present).
  if (s.has_need("args")) {
    s = s.write("    .section .bss\n");
    s = s.write("    .align 8\n");
    s = s.write("__fern_argc: .quad 0\n");
    s = s.write("    .align 8\n");
    s = s.write("__fern_argv: .quad 0\n");
    s = s.write("    .section .text\n");
